    <!--  Permission presets  -->
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Moe.Permission.RvmLabel">RVM isolation</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Moe.Permission.RvmDescription">Commands run on a dedicated session disk: workspace sources and configuration are selectively snapshotted by the Git index into local RVM storage and mounted as a drive; later starts only sync host-side changes. The real workspace directory is never granted to the sandbox, and temporary files go to a private Temp on the session disk. Choosing another level below disables isolation and restores the DSH sandbox.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Moe.Permission.SafeBadge">Safe</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Moe.Permission.AutoLabel">Auto review</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Moe.Permission.AutoDescription">Runs without a sandbox; the same model performs an experimental review before every native tool call and inner PTC call.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Moe.Permission.AutoConfirmDescription">Auto review does not use a sandbox. Before every native tool call and inner PTC call, the same model as the current agent reviews the call; calls rejected by review are approved or rejected by you. This feature is experimental, may allow or reject calls incorrectly, and consumes extra tokens.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Moe.Permission.FullAccessConfirmDescription">With full access, the agent skips more confirmation steps and can directly perform more operations, including sensitive actions, file modifications, and external commands. Use it only when you trust the current task.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Moe.Permission.ReadOnlyLabel">Read Only</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Moe.Permission.ReadOnlyDescription">Can read files; writes and modifications are denied by the sandbox</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Moe.Permission.WorkspaceWriteLabel">Workspace Write</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Moe.Permission.WorkspaceWriteDescription">Can read and write files inside the current workspace; modifications outside it are denied</sys:String>
