    <!--  RVM tab  -->
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Rvm.Title">RVM</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Rvm.Subtitle">Host components and grants that the sandbox depends on are managed here.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Rvm.SessionDiskTitle">Session disk and WinFsp</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Rvm.SessionDiskDesc">Protected sessions run on a session disk in local RVM storage: workspace sources and configuration are selectively snapshotted there by the Git index (dependency folders, build outputs, and caches are not copied); each later start only syncs host-side changes, while changes made inside the sandbox stay in the snapshot. Only this session disk is granted to the sandbox; the real workspace directory is never exposed. WinFsp 2.2 volume devices cannot be opened by an AppContainer (winfsp/winfsp#705), so the session disk is provided through a system drive mapping and WinFsp is only probed for installation.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Rvm.Status">Status: </sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Rvm.WinFspDiag">The probe result is diagnostic only; the session disk does not depend on WinFsp and will not fall back to the DSH sandbox when it is missing.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Rvm.WinFspInstalling">Installing WinFsp. Confirm the administrator prompt…</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Rvm.RecheckWinFsp">Recheck WinFsp</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Rvm.DriveLabel">Virtual drive</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Rvm.DriveHint">Preferred drive letter for the session disk; if it is in use, the engine switches to another free letter.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Rvm.PenetrationTitle">Network and device penetration</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Rvm.PenetrationDesc">Penetration policy is fixed into AppContainer capabilities and device ACLs when a session is created. Port masking is fixed: host loopback ports and session inbound ports are mutually invisible. Enabling network only allows outbound connections and does not lift masking. Network audit samples the host TCP/UDP tables for the command process tree and writes newly observed outbound endpoints to network.log in the session archive.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Rvm.Network">Network penetration</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Rvm.NetworkDesc">Off by default: the session has no network capability. When enabled, only the internetClient outbound capability is granted; no loopback exemption or inbound capability is granted, so host service ports remain masked.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Rvm.Devices">Device penetration</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Rvm.DevicesDesc">Only selected serial ports are exposed. The engine adds a read/write ACE for the session identity to the device security descriptor and removes it when the session stops. If a device cannot be opened or granted, session startup fails instead of pretending it was exposed.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Rvm.SerialPorts">Available serial ports</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Rvm.EnumPorts">Re-enumerate serial ports</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Rvm.NoSerial">No serial ports detected.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Rvm.PolicyPath">Policy is stored in %APPDATA%\Responsible\rvm-policy.json and applies the next time a protected session starts.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Rvm.ArchiveTitle">Session archive</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Rvm.ArchiveDesc">Session disk differences are measured against the local snapshot archive: startup records the clean host copy and system metadata (OS version, VBS/HVCI state, AppContainer identity, grants, environment variable names, tool directories), then only the session disk is traversed, never the host directory. Review, then sync or roll back. Sync writes back only non-conflicting items; rollback restores only the session disk and leaves host files untouched.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Rvm.RecheckSession">Reload session state</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Rvm.ArchiveBusy">Reading or writing the session archive…</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Rvm.Audit">Audit changes</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Rvm.Sync">Sync to local</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Rvm.Rollback">Roll back session disk</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Rvm.ArchiveEmpty">The session disk matches the baseline; no pending changes.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Rvm.ArchivePathHint">Snapshot archives are stored on this PC under %LOCALAPPDATA%\Responsible\RVM\&lt;storage key&gt;\: seed.manifest, baseline.manifest, system.json, system.log, audit.log. Read-only access to the host workspace never writes these files.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Rvm.AclTitle">ACL grants</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Rvm.AclDesc">Grant read/execute access on tool directories to the fixed RVM identity in one step. The grant writes a single inheritable ACE at the directory root, so existing and future files in the tree are covered automatically without changing their existing permissions.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Rvm.AddTool">Add tool directory</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Rvm.NoTools">No tool directories are granted yet. Add one below, then select the tools this session may use in the workspace settings.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Rvm.RemoveGrant">Remove grant</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Rvm.AclHint1">Grants are revalidated on every start. Invalid items are struck through; use the refresh button to regrant or remove them.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Rvm.AclHint2">Inherited grants live only at the directory root; tools installed or updated later need no regrant.</sys:String>

